The following (trivial) example fails with a 'Java heap space' error on my hadoop cluster (10 node Hortonworks HDP 2.1.2, hadoop 2.4.0):

# This part works:
tmpData <- to.dfs(1:10)

# this part fails
out2 <- mapreduce(
  input = tmpData,
  map = function(k,v) return(keyval(v, v^2)),
  reduce = to.reduce(identity))

# The same code with no reducer does not fail at all:
out1 <- mapreduce(
  input = tmpData,
  map = function(k,v) return(keyval(v, v^2)))

When the code with the reducer fails, the logs look like this (just one of them, they all look exactly the same):

