Not the most informative of messages, but if f is not properly initialized that will happen. I assume you run hdfs.init() Next thing would be to check that the path is correct. Does the example on our wiki page work for you? This is one possible version.

> model <- lm(mpg~cyl, data = mtcars)
> modelfilename <- "my_smart_unique_name"
> modelfile <- hdfs.file(modelfilename, "w")
> hdfs.write(model, modelfile)
[1] TRUE
> hdfs.close(modelfile)
[1] TRUE
> modelfile = hdfs.file(modelfilename, "r")
> m <- hdfs.read(modelfile)
> model <- unserialize(m)
> hdfs.close(modelfile)

